LAST_SUCCESS=Task 22 verified OK — rsbinder reaches SurfaceFlingerAIDL (android.gui.ISurfaceComposer) on Pixel 2 XL. Transport validated; service responds with structured Status (EX_NULL_POINTER on getPhysicalDisplayIds is a device-specific service-side rejection that matches what `adb shell service call SurfaceFlingerAIDL 4` returns — not a transport bug).
NOTES=Path: 1) new vendor/aosp-frameworks-native submodule sparse-checked-out to libs/gui/aidl/ + libs/gui/android/gui/ (324 KB). 2) build.rs self-heals two files: DisplayBrightness.aidl (0f/-1f float literals not parseable by rsbinder-aidl 0.7.0 → empty stub) and ISurfaceComposer.aidl (huge upstream → trimmed to first 4 methods preserving transaction codes). 3) display_impl.rs probes on cold-start via rsbinder::hub::get_interface("SurfaceFlingerAIDL"). EX_NULL_POINTER is consistent across our app and adb-shell shell user — service-side behavior on this LineageOS android-15-r36 SF build. Boot-model migration (§6.1) will need to use methods that don't NPE — likely higher-level SurfaceComposerClient or IDisplayManager.
